{
  "_comment": [
    "Restrictive seccomp allowlist for code-runner sandboxes.",
    "Forked from Docker's default seccomp profile (moby/moby:master/profiles/seccomp/default.json).",
    "Strategy: defaultAction SCMP_ACT_ERRNO (deny everything), explicit allow-list of syscalls",
    "needed by interpreted/compiled language runtimes.",
    "",
    "REMOVED from Docker default (dangerous syscalls untrusted code must never reach):",
    "  ptrace         -- process tracing / debugger attach, container breakout vector",
    "  mount          -- mount arbitrary filesystems, container escape",
    "  umount2        -- unmount, paired with mount; not needed",
    "  keyctl         -- Linux kernel keyring, credential theft",
    "  add_key        -- add keys to kernel keyring",
    "  request_key   -- request keys from kernel keyring",
    "  bpf            -- eBPF programs, kernel-level code execution / data exfil",
    "  clone3         -- new clone API with namespace flags (use plain clone for threads)",
    "  unshare        -- create new namespaces; not needed inside a container",
    "  setns          -- join namespaces; container breakout vector",
    "  kexec_load     -- load a new kernel; catastrophic",
    "  perf_event_open -- performance counters, side-channel attacks",
    "  userfaultfd    -- user-space page-fault handler, used in container escape exploits",
    "",
    "NOTE ON USAGE: dockerd (not the worker process) reads this file at container creation",
    "time. The path passed via SecurityOpt (e.g. 'seccomp=/etc/runner/seccomp.json') must",
    "be resolvable by the Docker daemon, not just the worker. Mount this file into the worker",
    "container and reference its in-container path, or use a host path accessible to dockerd.",
    "Reference: plan 02-01 Task 1; see STACK.md seccomp deep-dive."
  ],
